1 for a classroom consequence."},{"n":43,"t":"assess_parts","p":"A stem-and-leaf diagram of 20 masses, in grams, begins:\n\n2 | 1 4\n3 | 0 2 2 5 8\n4 | 1 4 6 9\n5 | 0 3\nKey: 3 | 2 means 32 g\n\n(a) State the smallest mass.\n(b) State how many masses are in the 40s.\n(c) State the mode.\n(d) A student says the median is 45. Without recalculating, explain why this cannot be correct.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A stem-and-leaf diagram of 20 masses, in grams, begins:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2 | 1 4\n3 | 0 2 2 5 8\n4 | 1 4 6 9\n5 | 0 3\nKey: 3 | 2 means 32 g"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(a) State the smallest mass.\n(b) State how many masses are in the 40s.\n(c) State the mode.\n(d) A student says the median is 45. Without recalculating, explain why this cannot be correct."}]}]},"e":"Smallest 21; four values in the 40s; mode 32. For n = 20 the median is the average of the 10th and 11th values, so it is not simply read off one leaf, and 45 does not correspond to the leaves at those positions.","m":6,"df":"hard","tp":"stem-and-leaf diagrams","st":"stem-and-leaf diagrams","cfg":{"source":"myp-mock-myp4-mock","question_number":43,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"C","strand":"C(i)","next_time_hint":"Locate the median by position (n/2), not by eye. For an even n the median need not be a data value.","assessment_style":"myp_mock","mock_exam_key":"myp4-mock","parts":[{"id":"a","label":"(a)","prompt":"State the smallest mass, in grams.","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Read the key: the stem gives the tens.","The first leaf in the diagram is on stem 2."],"strand":"C(i)","answer":21,"tolerance":0,"unit":"g"},{"id":"b","label":"(b)","prompt":"State how many masses are in the 40s.","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Every leaf on stem 4 is a mass in the forties.","Count the leaves 1, 4, 6 and 9."],"strand":"C(i)","answer":4,"tolerance":0},{"id":"c","lab